Perish.; Perire.

@AC 59[2]. If the Lord did not protect man every moment... he would at once perish...

@1874[end]. Thus the sense of the letter perishes as it ascends... @1875. @2015.

@1990[3]. (If the Lord had not assumed the Human) man would have perished to eternity in the death of the damned.

@2243[7]. So that the human race would have perished, because there was no Church...

@2253. Intercession from love that the human race should not perish. Signified, Explained.

@2256[2]. So that not the least (of the good, or evil, which man has thought or done, from infancy to the end of his life) completely perishes...

