@2268. Shall man perish for a little which is lacking? Signified, Explained.

@2269. He shall not perish if (good and truth) can be conjoined. Signified, Explained.

@2395. To "destroy," when predicated of the Lord, = to perish by evil; that is, to be damned.

@2397. That they cannot but perish. Signified, Explained.

@--. As they perished... through the Advent of the Lord into the world, it is said (thus) according to the appearance. @2402.

@2408. Lest they should perish in the evils of falsity. Signified.

@2457. Otherwise all those who are here represented by Lot would also have perished. Signified, Explained.

@2687. To "see death" = to perish.

@2754[end]. (These cruel adulterers) account it as nothing if the universal world were to perish for them.

@2912. A new Church in place of the former which has perished...

@2959. When the Church completely perishes...

@3116[end]. If the least of falsity were conjoined with good, or the least of truth with evil, the man would perish to eternity; for he would hang in the other life between Hell and Heaven...

@3340[end]. Unless this fury (of the Hells) were continually repelled by the Lord, the whole human race would perish.

@3387. Good is said to be "slain," or to perish, when it is not received...

@3938[4]. They believe that if they were deprived of (the delights of the affections of evil and falsity) they would altogether perish.

@4217[3]. (Without these external bonds) the human race would perish.

@4257[end]. Man perishes completely, when the Church... with him perishes. Signified, Explained.

@4288[end]. Without the communication of Heaven with man through something of the Church, the human race would perish.

@4423. Cannot apprehend but that those of the Old Church... will perish, as did the Antediluvians, and the Jews... But, when the Church has been vastated... it perishes principally as to the states of its interior things...

@4493[5]. Would have perished to eternity.

@4519. To perish. Signified.

@4687[2]. Thus the human race would perish.

@4785. That the Ancient Church was perishing. Signified.

@4847. Fear lest the representative of a Church should perish. Signified, Explained.

@5302. Lest man should perish by the defect of truth. Signified, Explained.

@5360[2]. "The day when the earth will perish." Explained.

@7655. To "perish" (Exodus 10:7) = to be cast into Hell.

@7879[2]. If the Hells were opened, the universal human race would perish...

@8699. That thus the truth which has been inseminated would perish. Signified, Explained.

