@9206. That the goods with them will perish. Signified, Explained.

@--[2]. Therefore, when the truth with man perishes, the good also perishes.

@9207. That truths will perish at the same time. Signified, Explained.

@9457[6]. Without the conjunction of the Lord through Heaven, man would perish.

@10276[end]. On the breaking (of the communication with the Heavens through the Word) the human race in this Earth would perish. Explained. @HH 305. [Swedenborg footnote 1.]

@10438. That those in good would perish. Signified, Explained.

@10452[3]. If the (Word) were not in the world, the conjunction with Heaven would perish; and with this conjunction, all the good of the will, and the truth of the understanding with man; and, with these, that human itself which consociates man with man...

@10506. That those who avert themselves from the Divine, will perish. Signified, Explained.

@10533. That if the internal were opened with that nation, and the Divine were to inflow, they would utterly perish. Signified, Explained.

@10632[end]. Without conjunction through such a Word, Heaven would completely recede from man, and thus man would perish.

@10791. If (order is not kept by prefects) the human race will perish. Explained.

